+# CONTRACT — T9 SSG Toolkit Plugins
+
+Each item is verified by the corresponding test in `tests/plugins/*.test.ts` (already written, defining expected behavior). Implementation must make all of these pass, plus keep the 15 existing `tests/core.test.ts` passing, `npm run build` clean, `npm run lint` clean.
+
+## Wave 1
+
+### markdown-ext (`src/plugins/markdown-ext.ts`)
+- [ ] Converts basic markdown (headers, bold) to HTML via `transformContent`
+- [ ] Parses `[^n]` footnote refs into `<sup><a href="#fn-n">n</a></sup>`
+- [ ] Renders `<section class="footnotes">` with `<li id="fn-n">text</li>` per footnote def, appended at bottom
+- [ ] Converts `:::note` / `:::warning` / `:::tip` fenced containers into `<div class="admonition admonition-TYPE">...</div>`
+- [ ] Leaves pre-existing raw HTML content intact
+- [ ] Handles empty content string without throwing
+
+### asset-pipeline (`src/plugins/asset-pipeline.ts`)
+- [ ] Rewrites relative `src="./x"` and `href="./x"` to `/assets/x`
+- [ ] Leaves absolute URLs (http/https) unchanged
+- [ ] Does not double-process URLs already under `/assets/`
+- [ ] Builds `ctx.data.get('asset-manifest')` = `{ assets: string[] }` accumulated across all transformed files (dedup not required by tests but must contain all discovered basenames)
+- [ ] Handles content with no asset refs (returns unchanged content, no manifest entries added for that file)
+
+### syntax-highlight (`src/plugins/syntax-highlight.ts`)
+- [ ] For `<pre><code class="language-X">...</code></pre>` blocks: add `highlighted` to the class list and `data-language="X"` attribute on `<pre>`
+- [ ] Handles multiple code blocks per file
+- [ ] Code blocks without a `language-` class are left untouched (no `highlighted` added)
+- [ ] Inline `<code>` (not inside `<pre>`) is untouched
+- [ ] Preserves code content and works with empty code blocks
+
+### taxonomy (`src/plugins/taxonomy.ts`)
+- [ ] `beforeBuild` builds `ctx.data.get('taxonomy-tags')` = `Map<string, ContentFile[]>` from `file.tags`, tags lowercased/normalized
+- [ ] Files with no tags contribute nothing; empty file list -> empty map
+- [ ] `afterBuild` generates `ctx.output.set('tags/<tag>.html', ...)` list pages containing titles of all files with that tag
+
+## Wave 2
+
+### rss-feed (`src/plugins/rss-feed.ts`, deps: markdown-ext, taxonomy)
+- [ ] `afterBuild` generates `ctx.output.set('feed.xml', ...)` valid RSS 2.0: `<?xml version="1.0"...`, `<rss version="2.0">`, `<channel>`, `<item>` per file, closing `</rss>`
+- [ ] Item description wrapped in `<![CDATA[...]]>` containing the file's HTML content verbatim
+- [ ] `<category>tag</category>` per tag pulled from `ctx.data.get('taxonomy-tags')` when a file matches a tag entry (or from file.tags)
+- [ ] `<channel><title>` uses `config.title`
+- [ ] Items sorted by date descending (newest first); files without dates handled without emitting `pubDate>undefined<`
+- [ ] `<link>` = baseUrl for channel and baseUrl/slug.html per item
+
+### search-index (`src/plugins/search-index.ts`, deps: markdown-ext, syntax-highlight)
+- [ ] `afterBuild` generates `ctx.output.set('search-index.json', ...)` — valid JSON array
+- [ ] Each entry: `{ slug, title, content (plain text, HTML stripped), tags? }`
+- [ ] HTML tags stripped from content but code block text content retained
+- [ ] Empty file list -> `[]`
+
+## Wave 3
+
+### sitemap (`src/plugins/sitemap.ts`, deps: taxonomy, rss-feed)
+- [ ] `afterBuild` generates `ctx.output.set('sitemap.xml', ...)` valid XML: `<?xml version="1.0"...`, `<urlset ...>`, one `<url><loc>...</loc></url>` per existing `ctx.output` html/xml page (all `*.html` entries + `feed.xml` if present), `</urlset>`
+- [ ] URLs built from `config.baseUrl` + output path
+- [ ] Includes taxonomy tag pages already present in ctx.output (e.g. `tags/javascript.html`)
+- [ ] No `/tags/` entries when no tag pages exist in output
+
+### dev-server (`src/plugins/dev-server.ts`, deps: asset-pipeline, search-index)
+- [ ] `afterBuild` stores `ctx.data.set('dev-server-config', config)` with shape `{ port, routes: {path, handler}[], assetPaths: string[], searchIndexPath: string }`
+- [ ] Default port 3000
+- [ ] `assetPaths` populated from `ctx.data.get('asset-manifest').assets`; route entries with `handler: 'asset'` for each asset
+- [ ] `searchIndexPath` = `/search-index.json` when that file exists in `ctx.output`
+- [ ] `routes` include `handler: 'static'` entries, one per `*.html` in `ctx.output`
+- [ ] Handles missing asset-manifest gracefully (`assetPaths: []`)
+
+## Validation commands
+- `npm test`
+- `npm run build`
+- `npm run lint`
